# Pinned to the PyPI release rather than a GitHub source archive: GitHub
# generates `archive/<sha>.tar.gz` on demand and does not guarantee the gzip
# bytes are stable, so a --require-hashes install against one breaks without
# warning when the archive is re-compressed. PyPI artifacts are immutable.
gnosis-mcp[embeddings]==0.17.5
